irst-person passage I could quote.\n\n**Passages I coded:** two topics have a passage, both from the issues page (snapshot `65ec3ff1`).\n- **`economic-development`:** the page says she will \"cut bureaucratic red tape\". This topic accepts own words only at the federal level, and that line is not her own words. It also says nothing about tax breaks or subsidies to attract companies, which is what this ladder ranks. Coded `adjacent`, `rhetorical`, `undated`.\n- **`religious-freedom`:** the page calls her a defender of \"the right to worship freely\". It names no rule on religious exemptions from anti-discrimination law. Coded `adjacent`, `rhetorical`, `undated`.\n\nThe other 17 topics have no passage, because the page doesn't address them.\n\n**What each row needs:** every row has a `needs_source` entry. For most topics that is her own first-person words, or a House roll call or sponsorship on a matching bill. For `ranked-choice-voting` I also listed her Indiana State Senate record. That is a hedge: a state-legislature record counts as `pre-seating` for her current House seat, not as an in-term record.\n\nNo row has a quote, because the page contains no first-person words of hers.","ttft_ms":16402,"type":"result","duration_ms":90254,"uuid":"eddba923-3b6b-4cb4-91a5-d7a2c10edd44","ttft_stream_ms":11023,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":11023,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
